 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2019-04-11",
   "text": "Consumer Health Insurance Protection Act of 2019\n\n This bill makes various changes to the health insurance marketplace, including (1) providing authority for the Department of Health and Human Services, or states, to prohibit health insurers from implementing unreasonable premium increases; (2) revising certain limits on cost sharing; and (3) modifying certain consumer protections."
  }
